Loom Code uses @earendil-works/pi-ai and @earendil-works/pi-tui, both
licensed under the MIT License and authored by Mario Zechner and contributors.
Their licenses remain applicable to those dependencies.

Loom's terminal view-state store uses Zustand, licensed under the MIT License.
Its license remains applicable to that dependency.

Loom's optional Cua integration uses @modelcontextprotocol/client,
licensed under the MIT License. Its license remains applicable to that
dependency. Cua Driver is an independently installed, MIT-licensed executable;
Loom does not bundle it or the separate Cua Spaces runtime.

Loom also uses @anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime, authored by Anthropic PBC
and licensed under Apache-2.0. Its license remains applicable to that
dependency; Loom's own source remains MIT-licensed.

Architecture research also consulted Pi, OpenAI Codex, OpenCode, and publicly
documented Claude Code behavior. Loom's orchestration core is implemented here;
Claude Code's private runtime was not inspected or incorporated.

See docs/architecture.md for the sources and implementation boundaries.
